   "text": {
    "L1": "A view shows an object from one direction. It is a flat outline, not a picture at an angle.",
    "L2": "Look straight down from above for the top view. Look straight at the object for the front view.",
    "L3": "For a glass, the top view shows its round mouth, so it is a circle.",
    "L4": "The front view shows the glass's height and width, so it is a rectangle.",
    "L5": "Here is the myth: a cylinder has a rectangle as its top view. That is not true.",
    "L6": "A cylinder and a cone can both look like circles from the top. We use more views to identify the object.",
    "L7": "Now check yourself: choose the top view of the glass."
   },
